{"stage": "review", "action": "scientific_findings", "result": {"verdict": "revise", "findings": ["Control type 'range' is unsupported by the lesson schema (execution_failures confirms two range controls fail). Replace c and eta controls with supported type 'number' (or the schema's supported slider type) so the lesson executes.", "The 'Regime' metric stores a string in metrics[3].value, but the schema/tests treat metric values as numbers; a string-valued metric is not numerically checkable and breaks the uniform metrics contract. Move regime to a separate string field (e.g. message/regime) and keep metrics numeric.", "The regime classification uses a fixed absolute tolerance 1e-12 on r and |r|. Because r = 1 - eta*c is computed in floating point, eta*c values that are mathematically exactly 1 or 2 (e.g. c=0.1, eta=10 not reachable, but c=0.3, eta=... ) may land slightly off and be misclassified. More importantly, the boundary eta*c=2 with c=1, eta=2 gives r=-1 exactly, fine, but c=0.5, eta=4 (eta max 3 so unreachable) — still, tolerance should be relative to |eta*c|, not absolute on r.", "The objective-curve x-range uses lo=min(-2, x0-1, finalX-1) and hi=max(2, x0+1, finalX+1). For divergent cases finalX can be enormous (e.g. eta*c=3, x0=1 → x12=4096), producing a plot dominated by the final point and a parabola sampled over a huge range, making the trajectory visually useless. Clamp the plotting window to a reasonable multiple of x0 (or the first few iterates).", "The 'iterates' series includes all 13 points (t=0..12) but the table only covers 12 steps; this is consistent, but the bar chart labels 't=0'..'t=12' (13 bars) while the description says 'step 0 to step 12' — acceptable, but the plan says 'first 12 iterates'; minor inconsistency between plan wording and 13 plotted points.", "No input validation: x0 can be 0 (allowed, stays 0) but the intro/help says 'finite nonzero'; the excerpt's convergence claim is for nonzero x0. Zero is handled correctly by the recurrence, so this is only a wording issue, not a numerical bug.", "The 'one-step convergence' regime is detected via |r-1|<1e-12, i.e. eta*c≈0, which is the eta*c=1 case (r=0). This is correct, but the label 'one-step convergence' is only exact when r=0; near r=0 (e.g. eta*c=0.999999) the message still claims exact one-step convergence. Tighten or reword."], "reference_tests": [{"name": "One-step convergence eta*c=1", "state": {"x0": 1, "c": 1, "eta": 1}, "expect": [{"path": "metrics.0.value", "value": 0, "atol": 1e-12}, {"path": "metrics.1.value", "value": 0, "atol": 1e-12}, {"path": "metrics.2.value", "value": 0, "atol": 1e-12}]}, {"name": "Constant oscillation eta*c=2", "state": {"x0": 1, "c": 1, "eta": 2}, "expect": [{"path": "metrics.0.value", "value": -1, "atol": 1e-12}, {"path": "metrics.1.value", "value": 1, "atol": 1e-12}, {"path": "metrics.2.value", "value": 0.5, "atol": 1e-12}]}, {"name": "Divergence eta*c=3", "state": {"x0": 1, "c": 1, "eta": 3}, "expect": [{"path": "metrics.0.value", "value": -2, "atol": 1e-12}, {"path": "metrics.1.value", "value": 4096, "atol": 1e-09}, {"path": "metrics.2.value", "value": 8388608, "atol": 0.001}]}, {"name": "Edge: zero start stays zero", "state": {"x0": 0, "c": 1, "eta": 0.5}, "expect": [{"path": "metrics.1.value", "value": 0, "atol": 1e-12}, {"path": "metrics.2.value", "value": 0, "atol": 1e-12}]}, {"name": "Edge: negative x0, alternating convergence", "state": {"x0": -2, "c": 1, "eta": 1.5}, "expect": [{"path": "metrics.0.value", "value": -0.5, "atol": 1e-12}, {"path": "metrics.1.value", "value": 0.00048828125, "atol": 1e-12}]}], "invariants": [{"name": "Linear recurrence: each iterate equals r times previous", "expression": "(()=>{const r=1-s.eta*s.c;const xs=o.panels[2].rows.map(row=>row[1]);const xsNext=o.panels[2].rows.map(row=>row[4]);return xs.every((x,i)=>Math.abs(xsNext[i]-r*x)<1e-9);})()"}, {"name": "Gradient equals c times iterate", "expression": "(()=>{const rows=o.panels[2].rows;return rows.every(row=>Math.abs(row[2]-s.c*row[1])<1e-9);})()"}, {"name": "Update equals -eta times gradient", "expression": "(()=>{const rows=o.panels[2].rows;return rows.every(row=>Math.abs(row[3]+s.eta*row[2])<1e-9);})()"}, {"name": "Final iterate equals r^12 times x0", "expression": "(()=>{const r=1-s.eta*s.c;return Math.abs(o.steps[2].value-Math.pow(r,12)*s.x0)<1e-6*Math.max(1,Math.abs(Math.pow(r,12)*s.x0));})()"}, {"name": "Objective equals c*x^2/2 at final iterate", "expression": "(()=>{const xf=o.steps[2].value;return Math.abs(o.metrics[2].value-s.c*xf*xf/2)<1e-6*Math.max(1,Math.abs(s.c*xf*xf/2));})()"}]}, "elapsed_seconds": 24.567}
